DIFR time-series implementation

Adapted from Deep Isolation Forest by Hongzuo Xu, Guansong Pang, Yijie Wang,
and Yongjun Wang: https://github.com/xuhongzuo/deep-iForest
Reference commit: e77692bbb39c851a580c37154c0a7d0c3a460bdf
Original algorithm source identifies Xu Hongzuo (hongzuo.xu@gmail.com),
2022/8/19, as its author. The original repository is licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0; the full license is included in LICENSE.

Modified for this reproduction:
- Keep only the time-series dilated residual CNN and isolation forest path.
- Supply all model settings from config.toml through the adapter.
- Generate the same full windows lazily and accumulate sparse decision paths.
- Use the approved paper Eq. (8) across all representation trees, raw traversed
  edge lengths, and Eq. (7)'s mean over all visited split nodes, including zeros.
- Keep collection-specific StandardScaler followed by tanh exactly as in the
  official representation extraction; do not read labels or adjust scores.
- Return the window-end score suffix and let the fixed evaluator align it.

The deliberate scoring differences from the official implementation and
neutral edge-case conventions are documented in the reproduction contract
and harness notes.
